course: dictionary
lesson: 7329
title: Planetary: planets and the whole world
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Planetary» is an adjective. It tells you what kind of thing something is, and it has two meanings. The first is to do with planets. «Venus is almost the same size as the Earth and is our nearest planetary neighbour» means Venus is a neighbouring planet in space.
explain: The second meaning is bigger: to do with the whole Earth, affecting the whole world. Scientists talk about a «planetary crisis» when a problem affects every person and every place on Earth, not just one town. Look at the words around it to choose the right meaning.
explain: Some planetary words are names for things that are not really about planets. A «planetary nebula» got its name because it looked like a round planet in old telescopes, but it has nothing to do with planets. When a word seems strange, check the context and, if you need to, a dictionary.
fact: Planetary means to do with planets.
fact: Planetary can also mean to do with the whole Earth, affecting the whole world.
fact: A «planetary system» is a star with planets going around it.
fact: «On a planetary scale» means across the whole world or the whole Solar System, not just in one place.
fact: A «planetary nebula» has nothing to do with planets; it got the name because it looked like a round planet in old telescopes.
exercise: «Venus is almost the same size as the Earth and is our nearest planetary neighbour.» What does planetary mean here? | A neighbour who lives on a farm | A neighbour who is very loud | *A planet that is a close neighbour of ours in space | A neighbour from another country
exercise: Scientists talk about a «planetary crisis». What does it mean? | A crisis on a spaceship only | *A problem that affects the whole Earth | A problem with one small village | A problem with the weather in one town
exercise: «A planetary system is a star with planets around it.» What is a planetary system? | A group of farms in the countryside | A system of trains that run around a city | A computer game about space | *A star with planets going around it
test: «The problem was on a planetary scale.» What does this mean? | *It affected the whole world | It was about cooking | Very small, in just one room | It happened only at night
test: Sam says «planetary nebula» means a glowing shell made of planets. Why is Sam wrong? | A nebula is a kind of planet | Sam is right, and no more explanation is needed | *It has nothing to do with planets; it looked like a round planet in old telescopes | Planets are made of glowing shells
exam: In «planetary health», what does planetary mean? | Happening only at night | *To do with the whole Earth and affecting everyone | Something only to do with cooking | Very tiny and hard to see
